---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspe1510.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope — the Classified Balance Sheet Distinction" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Definition of Current Assets" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Definition of Current Liabilities" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Segregation Into Main Classes" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. THE DISTINCTIVE RULE — Callable Debt Following a Covenant Violation" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Refinancing After the Balance Sheet Date" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. The Normal Operating Cycle" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Classifying Debt Callable Due to a Covenant Breach" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Worked Example — Refinancing Before the Financial Statements Are Completed" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Relationship to IAS 1's Current/Non-Current Classification" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "16. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The dividing line between short-term and long-term claims</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 1510 defines WHAT qualifies AS a CURRENT asset OR current LIABILITY — the DISTINCTION underlying the CLASSIFIED Balance SHEET presentation MOST ASPE preparers USE. THIS Section INCLUDES a GENUINELY distinctive rule GOVERNING debt SUBJECT to COVENANT violations (Section 6), WORTH particular ATTENTION given ITS practical SIGNIFICANCE for PRIVATE, lender-financed enterprises.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — the Classified Balance Sheet Distinction</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Applies wherever a classified presentation is used</div><div class="principle">This Section applies to ENTERPRISES presenting a CLASSIFIED Balance SHEET, DISTINGUISHING current FROM non-current ASSETS and LIABILITIES — the MOST common PRESENTATION approach FOR ASPE preparers, THOUGH an UNCLASSIFIED, liquidity-ORDERED presentation MAY be used WHERE it PROVIDES more RELIABLE and RELEVANT information.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Definition of Current Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cash, or realizable within one year or the operating cycle</div><div class="text-supporting">CURRENT assets COMPRISE cash, and OTHER assets that ARE readily CONVERTIBLE into a KNOWN amount OF cash, or ARE held for SALE or CONSUMPTION in the NORMAL course of OPERATIONS, WITHIN one YEAR from the BALANCE sheet date, OR within the NORMAL operating CYCLE when LONGER than a YEAR.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Definition of Current Liabilities</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Due within one year, the operating cycle, or on demand</div><div class="text-supporting">CURRENT liabilities COMPRISE liabilities DUE to be SETTLED within ONE year of the BALANCE sheet DATE (or the NORMAL operating CYCLE, when LONGER), AND liabilities that ARE payable ON demand.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Segregation Into Main Classes</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Presenting current items by major category</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Cash</span><span>Investments</span><span>Accounts and notes receivable</span><span>Inventories</span><span>Prepaid expenses</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>THE DISTINCTIVE RULE — Callable Debt Following a Covenant Violation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A covenant breach can force a current classification, even for long-term debt</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE long-TERM debt BECOMES callable BY the LENDER because OF a COVENANT violation — EVEN if the LENDER has NOT actually EXERCISED that RIGHT — the DEBT is GENERALLY classified as CURRENT, UNLESS the LENDER has WAIVED, or SUBSEQUENTLY lost, the RIGHT to DEMAND repayment FOR a period of MORE than ONE year FROM the balance SHEET date, or the VIOLATION is CURED within a SPECIFIED grace PERIOD. THIS is a GENUINELY distinctive, PRACTICALLY significant rule — a SINGLE covenant BREACH can PUSH an ENTIRE long-term LOAN balance into CURRENT liabilities, MATERIALLY affecting WORKING capital presentation and LENDER covenant CALCULATIONS themselves.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Refinancing After the Balance Sheet Date</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A narrow exception where genuine long-term refinancing has occurred</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE debt that WOULD otherwise be CLASSIFIED as CURRENT (e.g. DUE to a MATURITY within ONE year, OR a COVENANT violation) is REFINANCED on a GENUINELY long-term BASIS AFTER the balance SHEET date but BEFORE the FINANCIAL statements are COMPLETED, it MAY still be CLASSIFIED as long-TERM, PROVIDED the SPECIFIC conditions FOR this treatment ARE met.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>The Normal Operating Cycle</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A longer-than-one-year measuring stick for certain industries</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE an ENTERPRISE'S normal OPERATING cycle EXCEEDS one YEAR (COMMON in SECTORS such as LONG-term construction OR certain MANUFACTURING processes), the CURRENT/non-current DISTINCTION is MEASURED against THAT longer OPERATING cycle, RATHER than a FLAT one-year THRESHOLD.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Classifying Debt Callable Due to a Covenant Breach</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A single breach reclassifies the entire balance</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A breached debt-to-equity covenant</div><div class="wk-body">A private company has a $6,000,000 term loan maturing in 4 years. At the balance sheet date, the company breaches a debt-to-equity covenant, giving the lender the contractual right to demand immediate repayment — a right the lender has not yet exercised or waived.</div><div class="wk-answer">DESPITE the LOAN'S 4-year CONTRACTUAL maturity, the COMPANY classifies the FULL $6,000,000 as a <strong>CURRENT liability</strong>, SINCE the LENDER retains the RIGHT to CALL the DEBT and has NEITHER waived NOR lost THAT right as OF the balance SHEET date.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — Refinancing Before the Financial Statements Are Completed</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A genuine long-term refinancing restores long-term classification</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Curing the breach through refinancing</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example, the company refinances the loan on a new, genuinely long-term basis 6 weeks after the balance sheet date, before its financial statements are completed, meeting the specific conditions required for long-term classification.</div><div class="wk-answer">GIVEN the QUALIFYING refinancing OCCURRED before the FINANCIAL statements were COMPLETED, the COMPANY may CLASSIFY the $6,000,000 as <strong>NON-CURRENT</strong> — the SUBSEQUENT refinancing RESTORES the LONG-term classification THAT would otherwise HAVE been LOST due to the COVENANT breach.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 1510 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Main classes of current assets and current liabilities, presented separately</span><span>Circumstances surrounding a covenant violation resulting in current classification of otherwise long-term debt</span><span>Details of any post-year-end refinancing supporting continued long-term classification</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a covenant violation genuinely gives the lender a callable right, and whether that right has been waived</span><span>Determining the length of an enterprise's normal operating cycle</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Generally minimal — this Section is primarily a classification standard</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 1's Current/Non-Current Classification</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 1510 vs IAS 1</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 1510</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 1</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>General current/non-current test</span><span>One year or operating cycle, if longer</span><span>Twelve months or operating cycle, if longer — converged in substance</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Callable debt due to covenant breach</span><span>Current, unless waived for over a year or cured within a grace period</span><span>Broadly similar principle, refined by amendments effective 2024</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">BROADLY converged in PRINCIPLE — the CALLABLE debt TREATMENT is CONCEPTUALLY similar to IFRS'S OWN approach, THOUGH the SPECIFIC mechanics and RECENT IFRS amendments SHOULD be COMPARED carefully IF precise CROSS-framework alignment MATTERS for a SPECIFIC fact PATTERN.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every current/non-current classification event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Covenant-triggered reclassification</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Moves debt from non-current to current presentation</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3210</span><span>Long-term Debt — supplies the general debt accounting this Section's classification rules apply to</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1521</span><span>Balance Sheet — governs the overall presentation this Section's current/non-current distinction feeds into</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Callable debt</div><div class="glossary-def">Debt subject to a lender's contractual right to demand immediate repayment, commonly triggered by a covenant violation, requiring current classification absent a waiver or cure.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Normal operating cycle</div><div class="glossary-def">The typical time span between the acquisition of materials for a process and their conversion into cash, used as the current/non-current threshold when longer than one year.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe1510 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
